# 必考词 Unit14
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit14核心词汇

{{damage}}{{/ˈdæmɪdʒ}}{{n./v. 损害；损失；赔偿金；伤害；破坏}}{{The storm caused serious damage to the buildings.}}
{{daring}}{{/ˈdeərɪŋ}}{{adj. 大胆的；勇敢的；敢于冒险的；鲁莽的}}{{The daring rescue saved the trapped miners.}}
{{deadline}}{{/ˈdedlaɪn}}{{n. 截止日期；最后期限；界限；期限}}{{The deadline for submitting the report is next Friday.}}
{{debate}}{{/dɪˈbeɪt}}{{n./v. 辩论；讨论；争论；考虑； deliberation}}{{The students held a debate on climate change.}}
{{decade}}{{/ˈdekeɪd}}{{n. 十年；十年期；年代；世纪}}{{The city has changed dramatically over the past decade.}}
{{decay}}{{/dɪˈkeɪ}}{{v./n. 腐烂；衰退；衰变；腐朽； decayed}}{{The old wooden house has begun to decay.}}
{{deceive}}{{/dɪˈsiːv}}{{v. 欺骗；蒙蔽；误导；行骗；诓骗}}{{He deceived everyone with his fake credentials.}}
{{decline}}{{/dɪˈklaɪn}}{{v./n. 下降；拒绝；衰退；倾斜；婉拒}}{{The company's profits have declined significantly.}}
{{dedicate}}{{/ˈdedɪkeɪt}}{{v. 奉献；致力于；题献； dedicating； dedication}}{{She dedicated her life to helping the poor.}}
{{deem}}{{/diːm}}{{v. 认为；视为；相信；觉得；估计}}{{The proposal was deemed unacceptable.}}
{{defect}}{{/ˈdiːfekt}}{{n. 缺点；缺陷；毛病；叛逃；变节}}{{The product was recalled due to a manufacturing defect.}}
{{deficit}}{{/ˈdefɪsɪt}}{{n. 赤字；不足；亏损； deficit；亏空}}{{The government is trying to reduce the budget deficit.}}
{{define}}{{/dɪˈfaɪn}}{{v. 定义；限定；解释；明确；界定}}{{How do you define success?}}
{{defy}}{{/dɪˈfaɪ}}{{v. 违抗；蔑视；使不可能；挑战； defy}}{{He defied all odds to achieve his dream.}}
{{degenerate}}{{/dɪˈdʒenəreɪt}}{{v./adj. 退化；堕落的；变质的；退化的}}{{The discussion degenerated into a shouting match.}}
{{deliberate}}{{/dɪˈlɪbərət}}{{adj./v. 故意的；深思熟虑的；审议；商议}}{{It was a deliberate attempt to mislead the public.}}
{{delicate}}{{/ˈdelɪkət}}{{adj. 精致的；脆弱的；微妙的；精细的；清淡的}}{{The vase is very delicate, so handle it with care.}}
{{demonstrate}}{{/ˈdemənstreɪt}}{{v. 展示；证明；示威；演示；示范}}{{The experiment demonstrates the effect of gravity.}}
{{denote}}{{/dɪˈnəʊt}}{{v. 表示；意味着；指示；代表；指的是}}{{The symbol 'π' denotes the ratio of circumference to diameter.}}
{{deny}}{{/dɪˈnaɪ}}{{v. 否认；拒绝；拒绝承认；拒绝给予； deniable}}{{He denied any involvement in the scandal.}}
{{depict}}{{/dɪˈpɪkt}}{{v. 描绘；描述；描画；刻画；表现}}{{The painting depicts a beautiful landscape.}}
{{deploy}}{{/dɪˈplɔɪ}}{{v. 部署；展开；利用；调动；有效使用}}{{The army deployed troops along the border.}}
{{deposit}}{{/dɪˈpɒzɪt}}{{n./v. 存款；押金；沉积；保证金；存放}}{{You need to pay a deposit when renting an apartment.}}
{{deprive}}{{/dɪˈpraɪv}}{{v. 剥夺；使丧失；使不能有；使贫困；夺去}}{{The war deprived many children of their education.}}
{{derive}}{{/dɪˈraɪv}}{{v. 源于；获得；得到；推导；导出}}{{The word is derived from Latin.}}
{{descend}}{{/dɪˈsend}}{{v. 下降；下来；遗传；是…的后裔；袭击}}{{The plane descended slowly through the clouds.}}
{{deserve}}{{/dɪˈzɜːv}}{{v. 应得；值得；应受；配得上；理应获得}}{{She deserves a promotion for her hard work.}}
{{design}}{{/dɪˈzaɪn}}{{n./v. 设计；计划；构思；企图；图案}}{{The architect presented the design for the new building.}}
{{desire}}{{/dɪˈzaɪər}}{{n./v. 渴望；欲望；要求；期望；请求}}{{He has a strong desire to succeed in life.}}
{{desperate}}{{/ˈdespərət}}{{adj. 绝望的；不顾一切的；极度渴望的；危急的；拼死的}}{{The refugees were in desperate need of food and water.}}
{{despite}}{{/dɪˈspaɪt}}{{prep. 尽管；不管；虽然；任凭；不顾}}{{Despite the rain, the event was a great success.}}
{{destiny}}{{/ˈdestɪni}}{{n. 命运；天命；定数；天数；命中注定的事}}{{She believed it was her destiny to become a teacher.}}
{{detect}}{{/dɪˈtekt}}{{v. 发现；探测；察觉；检测；侦查}}{{The sensor can detect changes in temperature.}}
{{deteriorate}}{{/dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt}}{{v. 恶化；变坏；退化；质量下降；堕落}}{{His health deteriorated rapidly after the diagnosis.}}
{{determine}}{{/dɪˈtɜːmɪn}}{{v. 决定；确定；查明；决心；限定}}{{Your attitude determines your altitude in life.}}
{{devastate}}{{/ˈdevəsteɪt}}{{v. 毁坏；使震惊；摧毁；使荒废；破坏}}{{The earthquake devastated the entire region.}}
{{devise}}{{/dɪˈvaɪz}}{{v. 设计；发明；想出；策划； devise a plan}}{{They devised a plan to solve the problem.}}
{{devote}}{{/dɪˈvəʊt}}{{v. 献身于；致力于；奉献；用于；投入}}{{She devoted her life to helping the poor.}}
{{diagnose}}{{/ˈdaɪəɡnəʊz}}{{v. 诊断；判断；分析；查明；确定病因}}{{The doctor diagnosed the illness as pneumonia.}}
{{dictate}}{{/dɪkˈteɪt}}{{v. 口述；命令；支配；听写；规定}}{{The manager dictated a letter to his secretary.}}
{{differ}}{{/ˈdɪfər}}{{v. 不同；意见不合；相异；有区别；持异议}}{{Opinions differ on how to solve the problem.}}
{{digest}}{{/daɪˈdʒest}}{{v./n. 消化；摘要；领悟；理解；文摘}}{{It takes time to digest a heavy meal.}}
{{dilemma}}{{/dɪˈlemə}}{{n. 进退两难；困境；两难选择；矛盾；窘境}}{{She faced a dilemma between career and family.}}
{{dimension}}{{/daɪˈmenʃn}}{{n. 维度；尺寸；方面；规模；大小}}{{The problem has several dimensions that need to be considered.}}
{{diminish}}{{/dɪˈmɪnɪʃ}}{{v. 减少；缩小；降低；贬低；削弱}}{{His influence has diminished over the years.}}
{{diplomat}}{{/ˈdɪpləmæt}}{{n. 外交官；善于交际的人；圆滑的人；外交家}}{{The diplomat negotiated a peace agreement.}}
{{discern}}{{/dɪˈsɜːn}}{{v. 辨别；识别；看出；察觉；分辨}}{{It is difficult to discern the truth from the lies.}}
{{discipline}}{{/ˈdɪsəplɪn}}{{n./v. 纪律；学科；训练；惩戒；自我控制}}{{Self-discipline is the key to success.}}
{{disclose}}{{/dɪsˈkləʊz}}{{v. 揭露；透露；公开；使显露；说出}}{{The company refused to disclose its financial information.}}
{{discount}}{{/ˈdɪskaʊnt}}{{n./v. 折扣；打折；忽视；低估；贴现}}{{The store offers a 20% discount on all items.}}
{{discourse}}{{/ˈdɪskɔːs}}{{n./v. 论述；演讲；话语；论文；讲述}}{{The professor delivered a discourse on modern philosophy.}}
{{discriminate}}{{/dɪˈskrɪmɪneɪt}}{{v. 歧视；区分；辨别；区别对待；有辨别力}}{{It is illegal to discriminate against people based on race.}}
{{discuss}}{{/dɪsˈkʌs}}{{v. 讨论；商议；论述；辩论；研讨}}{{Let's discuss the issue at the meeting.}}
{{disguise}}{{/dɪsˈɡaɪz}}{{v./n. 伪装；假扮；掩饰；化装用品；借口}}{{He disguised himself as a police officer.}}
{{dismiss}}{{/dɪsˈmɪs}}{{v. 解雇；驳回；不理会；开除；不予考虑}}{{The court dismissed the case due to lack of evidence.}}
{{disorder}}{{/dɪsˈɔːdər}}{{n. 混乱；疾病；骚乱；失调；无秩序}}{{The patient was diagnosed with a sleep disorder.}}
{{dispatch}}{{/dɪˈspætʃ}}{{v./n. 派遣；发送；调度；急件；迅速处理}}{{The goods were dispatched to the warehouse.}}
{{disperse}}{{/dɪˈspɜːs}}{{v. 分散；驱散；传播；疏散；散开}}{{The crowd dispersed after the concert ended.}}
{{displace}}{{/dɪsˈpleɪs}}{{v. 取代；迫使离开；使移位；置换；免职}}{{The flood displaced thousands of people from their homes.}}
{{display}}{{/dɪˈspleɪ}}{{v./n. 展示；显示；陈列；表现；展示品}}{{The museum displays artifacts from ancient civilizations.}}
{{dispose}}{{/dɪsˈpəʊz}}{{v. 处理；布置；使倾向于；处置；丢弃}}{{Please dispose of the waste properly.}}
{{dispute}}{{/dɪˈspjuːt}}{{n./v. 争论；纠纷；争端；质疑；争执}}{{The dispute between the two companies was settled in court.}}
{{disregard}}{{/ˌdɪsrɪˈɡɑːd}}{{v./n. 忽视；漠视；不尊重；不顾；不理}}{{He disregarded the warning and continued driving.}}
{{disrupt}}{{/dɪsˈrʌpt}}{{v. 扰乱；使中断；使混乱；破坏；妨碍}}{{The protest disrupted traffic in the city center.}}
{{dissolve}}{{/dɪˈzɒlv}}{{v. 溶解；解散；消失；解除；废除}}{{Sugar dissolves quickly in hot water.}}
{{distinct}}{{/dɪˈstɪŋkt}}{{adj. 明显的；不同的；独特的；清楚的；确切的}}{{There is a distinct difference between the two approaches.}}
{{distinguish}}{{/dɪˈstɪŋɡwɪʃ}}{{v. 区分；辨别；使杰出；辨认；看清}}{{It is hard to distinguish the twins from each other.}}
{{distort}}{{/dɪˈstɔːt}}{{v. 歪曲；扭曲；使变形；失真；曲解}}{{The media sometimes distorts the facts.}}
{{distract}}{{/dɪˈstrækt}}{{v. 分散注意力；使分心；使困惑；使烦恼；转移}}{{Noise distracts me from studying.}}
{{distribute}}{{/dɪˈstrɪbjuːt}}{{v. 分配；分发；散布；分销；分布}}{{The volunteers distributed food to the homeless.}}
{{disturb}}{{/dɪˈstɜːb}}{{v. 打扰；使不安；弄乱；干扰；妨碍}}{{Please do not disturb me while I am studying.}}
{{diverse}}{{/daɪˈvɜːs}}{{adj. 多样的；不同的；形形色色的；多种多样的；各种的}}{{The university has a diverse student body.}}
{{divert}}{{/daɪˈvɜːt}}{{v. 转移；使转向；消遣；使转移注意力；改道}}{{The river was diverted to prevent flooding.}}
{{divine}}{{/dɪˈvaɪn}}{{adj./n. 神圣的；非凡的；神的；天赐的；极好的}}{{The ancient Greeks believed in divine intervention.}}
{{doctrine}}{{/ˈdɒktrɪn}}{{n. 教义；学说；主义； doctrine；教条；信条}}{{The party's doctrine emphasizes individual freedom.}}
{{domain}}{{/dəˈmeɪn}}{{n. 领域；域；领地；范围；产业；域名}}{{She is an expert in the domain of artificial intelligence.}}
{{domestic}}{{/dəˈmestɪk}}{{adj. 国内的；家庭的；驯养的； domestic affairs；本国的}}{{Domestic flights are cheaper than international ones.}}
{{dominant}}{{/ˈdɒmɪnənt}}{{adj. 占主导地位的；显著的；优势的；统治的；支配的}}{{English is the dominant language in international business.}}
{{donate}}{{/dəʊˈneɪt}}{{v. 捐赠；捐献；献出；赠送；捐助}}{{He donated blood to the local hospital.}}
{{doom}}{{/duːm}}{{n./v. 厄运；注定；判决；末日；毁灭}}{{The project was doomed to fail from the start.}}
{{dose}}{{/dəʊs}}{{n. 剂量；一剂；一次；一份；一服}}{{The doctor prescribed a low dose of the medication.}}
{{draft}}{{/drɑːft}}{{n./v. 草稿；起草；草案；汇票；征兵}}{{She submitted the first draft of her thesis.}}
{{drain}}{{/dreɪn}}{{v./n. 排水；耗尽；下水道；消耗；引流}}{{The heavy rain drained the reservoir.}}
{{drastic}}{{/ˈdræstɪk}}{{adj. 激烈的；严厉的；极端的；猛烈的；急剧的}}{{The company took drastic measures to cut costs.}}
{{dread}}{{/dred}}{{n./v. 恐惧；担忧；害怕；忧虑；令人畏惧的事}}{{She dreads speaking in public.}}
{{drift}}{{/drɪft}}{{v./n. 漂流；漂移；趋势；大意；流动}}{{The boat drifted slowly down the river.}}
{{drought}}{{/draʊt}}{{n. 干旱；旱灾；缺乏；长期缺乏；干旱时期}}{{The severe drought destroyed the crops.}}
{{dub}}{{/dʌb}}{{v. 起绰号；配音；授予称号；称为；复制}}{{The media dubbed him the "King of Pop."}}
{{due}}{{/djuː}}{{adj. 到期的；应有的；由于；预定的；适当的}}{{The report is due by the end of this week.}}
{{dull}}{{/dʌl}}{{adj. 枯燥的；阴暗的；钝的；迟钝的；萧条的}}{{The lecture was so dull that many students fell asleep.}}
{{dump}}{{/dʌmp}}{{v./n. 倾倒；垃圾场；丢弃；倾销；甩掉}}{{It is illegal to dump waste in the river.}}
{{duplicate}}{{/ˈdjuːplɪkeɪt}}{{v./adj./n. 复制；重复的；副本；复制品；副本的}}{{Please duplicate this document for the meeting.}}
{{durable}}{{/ˈdjʊərəbl}}{{adj. 耐用的；持久的；坚固的；经久的；耐穿的}}{{This material is very durable and can last for years.}}
{{duration}}{{/djuˈreɪʃn}}{{n. 持续时间；期间；持久；持续；期限}}{{The duration of the flight is approximately three hours.}}
{{dynamic}}{{/daɪˈnæmɪk}}{{adj. 动态的；有活力的；动力的；不断变化的；充满活力的}}{{The city has a dynamic and vibrant culture.}}
